{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Retain the 5 year settlement pathway for all UK Skilled Workers",
        "additional_details": "While some current care workers and earners over \u00a350,271 will be able to keep the 5-year route, others who we see as the tax-paying \"missing middle\" face a decade of instability. We believe extending the wait to a decade of uncertainty, disrupting homeownership and family stability is unfair. We urge the Government to retain a fair, five-year pathway for all eligible migrants, as we feel permanent settlement should not be a privilege reserved only for the highest earners.",
        "background": "We urge the Government to retain a 5-year pathway for all skilled workers, including current visa holders and future applicants. We feel it is unfair that the Earned Settlement policy doubles the ILR wait to 10 years for many skilled workers. ",
